    "final_text": "I added the v2.4.0 (2026-10-20) release notes to the top of `RELEASE_NOTES.md`, just under the title, using the Acme house format:\n\n```\n## v2.4.0 (2026-10-20)\n\n### Breaking changes\n- None.\n\n### Features\n- Export reports to CSV straight from the report command [ACME-412] (thanks @mira)\n- Uploads now retry automatically with backoff when the server is temporarily unavailable (HTTP 503) [ACME-415] (thanks @jonas)\n\n### Fixes\n- An empty config file no longer causes a crash [ACME-419] (thanks @tom)\n- Monthly summaries now show correct totals in leap years [ACME-423] (thanks @priya)\n```\n\nACME-421 is left out as you asked. It was the only breaking change in the list (removing the `--legacy` flag from sync), so the Breaking changes section now just says \"None.\" The format requires that section to stay even when it's empty.\n\nThe older v2.3.0 and v2.2.0 entries are unchanged.",
